{"year":"2026","sessionID":"2026GS","sessionIndex":"1","billNumber":"HB0331","billNumberShort":"H.B. 331","billNumberLong":"HB0331S02","fileNumber":"2026FL1245","shortTitle":"Criminal Offenses Modifications","currentSubVersion":"2","currentMinVersion":"0","primeSponsor":"CLANCT","primeSponsorName":"Rep. Clancy, Tyler","primeSponsorHouse":"H","floorSponsor":"GROVEK","floorSponsorName":"Sen. Grover, Keith","floorSponsorHouse":"S","generalProvisions":"This bill addresses criminal offenses.","highlightedProvisions":"This bill:<hr><ltbullet>amends the offense of threat of terrorism by:<hr><ltbullet1>renaming the offense to terrorism; and<hr><ltbullet1>clarifying that the offense applies to certain completed acts in addition to threatened acts;<hr><ltbullet>creates the offense of unlawfully advancing foreign organizations and governments;<hr><ltbullet>creates the offense of intentional concealment of identity while committing an offense in public;<hr><ltbullet>creates the offense of unlawful deprivation of religious rights with a corresponding civil right of action by a victim that may be brought against the actor;<hr><ltbullet>amends the definition of unlawful activity applicable to the offense of prohibited conduct concerning a pattern of unlawful activity to include the offenses of aggravated disorderly conduct on a street or highway and unlawfully advancing foreign organizations and governments; and<hr><ltbullet>makes technical and conforming changes.","moniesAppropriated":"None","draftingAttorney":"Shad Larson","fiscalAnalyst":"Joseph Fitzgerald","lastAction":"Governor Signed","lastActionOwner":"Lieutenant Governor's office for filing","lastActionDate":"3/24/2026","trackingID":"TMYBDQVPUI","actionHistoryList":[{"description":"Bill Numbered but not Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2026-01-22 13:58:06.447","actionClass":"L","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LNUMBER","parm1":"","parm2":""},{